1
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:20,260
Okay, Hermes, how fast is
this thing going right now?

2
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:23,117
170? 200?

3
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:25,780
We're getting off of this thing! Emporio!

4
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:34,257
But when those rods came into my life
and I saw them for the first time,

5
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:36,340
I finally realized its importance.

6
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:37,971
It wasn't about the dude.

7
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:40,857
The moon landing was an
achievement for all humanity.

8
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:44,277
That day, we humans conquered
the moon and our spirits evolved.

9
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:48,460
What's truly significant is the
evolution of the human race!

10
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:51,920
You don't gotta worry about me.

11
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:54,440
I honestly don't even feel it.

12
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:57,697
Compared to all the shit I've
gone through to get to the priest,

13
00:00:57,780 --> 00:00:59,015
this pain is nothing.

14
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:02,960
You crazy bitch!

15
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:07,500
If you're trying to test my spirit,
it's way stronger than yours!

16
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:11,760
I'm gonna finish you here!

17
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:19,390
Aw, shit!

18
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:24,200
Jolene! Aw, yeah!

19
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:25,420
A girl's alive!

20
00:01:26,040 --> 00:01:29,917
He must be special since the priest
took away the disc with his memories.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,877
And he decided to keep him
alive in that prison...

22
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:34,960
Weather forecast.

23
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:40,533
Because he happens to be the
priest's biological brother.

24
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,780
Let's go! To Orlando!

25
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:45,791
That's where we'll find him hiding, right?

26
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:48,100
Destiny is mine!

27
00:02:03,060 --> 00:02:05,520
Thank you.

28
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:50,817
Thank you

29
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:55,097
so

30
00:02:55,180 --> 00:02:58,497
much

31
00:02:58,580 --> 00:02:59,680
for joining us.

32
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:03,179
That's it, though.

33
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:05,897
I don't want to be the one.

34
00:03:05,980 --> 00:03:07,860
I don't want to be the one.

35
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:19,054
It's not that the one.

36
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:23,375
I'm not that the one.

37
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:30,199
I'm not my friend.

38
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:39,430
Hurry!

39
00:03:39,513 --> 00:03:40,987
Get surgery room 3 prepared.

40
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:44,256
We've got an eight-year-old
boy in critical condition.

41
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:47,360
It's okay. It'll be okay.

42
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:52,440
Hey, Jolene.

43
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:54,697
You said this is where
the priest was hiding.

44
00:03:54,780 --> 00:03:56,604
But this is a fucking hospital?

45
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,350
He's here.

46
00:03:58,580 --> 00:04:02,480
I don't know why, but he's
definitely waiting for us inside.

47
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:06,754
We're going to put an end to this here.

48
00:04:13,260 --> 00:04:14,090
Emporio.

49
00:04:14,173 --> 00:04:15,003
I need a favor.

50
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,339
This is important.

51
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:19,817
I want you to take my father's
disc and deliver it for me.

52
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:23,900
If you call this number, the
Speedwagon Foundation will come get it.

53
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:30,460
I want to go in with you! I know.

54
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:33,817
But before that, I need you to
make sure the disc gets delivered.

55
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:35,018
It's all up to you.

56
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:38,137
By now, the priest should sense
that I'm getting closer to him.

57
00:04:38,220 --> 00:04:41,455
I don't want to be separated
from you right now either.

58
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:42,900
But it's necessary.

59
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:50,478
Keep in touch with this cell
phone I took off Rikiel.

60
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:11,640
Sorry to bother you,

61
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:14,357
but I'd like to hear your opinion
on something I'm unsure of,

62
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:16,060
particularly this dish.

63
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:17,791
Take a bite if you would.

64
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:19,939
I want you to taste test it for me.

65
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:21,790
Versus...

66
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:31,880
One bite is enough.

67
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:40,437
After you eat it, tell me
what ingredients are inside.

68
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:42,840
If there's shellfish, I can't eat it.

69
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:45,513
I'm allergic, so I would get quite sick.

70
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:52,500
This is whitefish.

71
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:55,080
Most likely, flounder.

72
00:05:56,360 --> 00:06:00,889
It has been paired with this flan, a
delectable pudding mixed with asparagus,

73
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,840
and mashed up crab meat inside.

74
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:05,420
I detect no shellfish.

75
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:07,590
Incredible.

76
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:09,340
But hold on a second.

77
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:14,297
May I have another small bite, but this
time with a little dab of sauce on the side?

78
00:06:14,380 --> 00:06:16,556
There's a faint scent from the sauce.

79
00:06:17,140 --> 00:06:21,493
Judging by the fishy aroma, I suspect
it's scallop paste mixed with cream.

80
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:31,037
How unfortunate?

81
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:34,397
Just as I thought, there are
scallops inside the sauce!

82
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:38,117
Is your shoe size 27 centimeters?

83
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:41,317
Pardon me, but could
you stand for a moment?

84
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:45,877
Be careful not to open up
the bullet wound on your leg.

85
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:47,017
Slowly now.

86
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:52,157
You're about 181 centimeters tall? Yes.

87
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:54,577
And you weigh precisely 72 kilograms?

88
00:06:54,660 --> 00:06:56,957
Are your clothes size 52?

89
00:06:57,040 --> 00:07:00,417
And do you tighten your watch
belt on the second hole?

90
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:01,517
Yes.

91
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:04,557
How interesting?

92
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:08,177
Though I'm unable to enjoy this fine meal.

93
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:11,897
I'm quite impressed by your ability to
pick out the scallop from the sauce.

94
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:16,020
It would appear we have
a similar sense of taste.

95
00:07:25,660 --> 00:07:26,617
Interesting indeed.

96
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:32,517
Tell me, Father Poochie,
what are you trying to say?

97
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:35,977
You're aware I haven't
seen my own ability yet?

98
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:39,766
And plus, I can sense someone
quickly approaching our location.

99
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,457
I want to help in any way I can.

100
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:44,357
What should I do?

101
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:45,597
Hmm.

102
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:48,560
That can't be helped.

103
00:07:49,180 --> 00:07:52,533
In fact, their arrival might
actually prove useful to me.

104
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:55,580
Oh, Mike.

105
00:07:55,980 --> 00:07:57,627
Your son's going to be fine.

106
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:01,080
He's really close now.

107
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:03,060
He's here somewhere.

108
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:06,977
If you're still unable
to see your ability,

109
00:08:07,060 --> 00:08:09,477
then there's nothing
else that can be done.

110
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:12,197
Don't struggle against things
beyond your understanding.

111
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:14,340
Let the power take its own course.

112
00:08:15,860 --> 00:08:18,036
If we are going to make it to heaven,

113
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:22,401
You must ally yourself with the
power that lies dormant within you.

114
00:08:23,020 --> 00:08:27,196
And besides, there's a chance Jolene
might overlook this room entirely.

115
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:28,830
Nevertheless,

116
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:33,297
I decided to order this dish because they
told me there'd be no shellfish inside.

117
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:35,674
If you'd like, you may eat it yourself.

118
00:08:39,660 --> 00:08:40,700
Father Pooji.

119
00:08:43,220 --> 00:08:45,780
I, uh, I...

120
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:49,190
I...

121
00:08:49,273 --> 00:08:50,680
I was...

122
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:53,817
Look at me!

123
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,280
I was shot to death!

124
00:08:56,620 --> 00:08:59,796
It was a lot of fun going
for a ride in the ambulance,

125
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:02,920
but it was ruined because
my daddy doesn't like me.

126
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:05,400
My daddy's the one who shot me!

127
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:08,080
He was trying to kill me!

128
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:12,957
Honey! Honey!

129
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:14,320
Honey, what happened?

130
00:09:14,640 --> 00:09:15,640
Someone was shot!

131
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:18,200
Oh, God! Why?

132
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:20,267
Why did you have to take it?

133
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:21,900
No! No!

134
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:31,957
What the hell?

135
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:33,920
This hospital room is a mess.

136
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:37,020
That priest must have been in here.

137
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:40,216
But now, where the fuck is he hiding?

138
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:43,257
Whatever's going on, I
think it's safe to assume?

139
00:09:43,340 --> 00:09:45,357
That the new enemy that's been
hanging around the priest.

140
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:46,911
is the cause of all this.

141
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:52,106
Although, that gunshot didn't
exactly feel like a stand attack.

142
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:54,848
It's more like somebody
fired a real bullet.

143
00:09:55,160 --> 00:09:57,157
And the poor bastard that got shot.

144
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:58,580
Who even is that guy?

145
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:00,737
Why would he be the one to get hit?

146
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:04,761
I mean, looking at him, he seems
to be just a random ordinary dude.

147
00:10:05,940 --> 00:10:08,757
I need you to hurry and
evacuate everyone on this floor.

148
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:10,200
Now! Yes, sir!

149
00:10:11,060 --> 00:10:13,119
Hey, that goes for you two as well!

150
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:14,537
Hurry up and evacuate!

151
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:16,502
I'm going to go call the police!

152
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:20,470
That's right.

153
00:10:20,553 --> 00:10:21,897
I remember that man now.

154
00:10:21,980 --> 00:10:23,757
He's the parent of that
kid who was brought in

155
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:26,722
by the ambulance when we
first got to this place.

156
00:10:27,380 --> 00:10:29,500
Maybe it was a test shot. Huh?

157
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:33,637
I have no idea what kind
of ability it could be,

158
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:36,737
but if it's someone who just
had their powers awakened,

159
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:41,114
they would need to give it a test
drive and try it out on somebody first.

160
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:53,680
The priest is moving right now.

161
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,195
Somewhere down there.

162
00:10:55,380 --> 00:10:57,017
That bastard's inside the hole.

163
00:10:57,100 --> 00:10:59,865
I can sense him getting
further away from here.

164
00:11:08,740 --> 00:11:09,880
Come on, Jolene.

165
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:12,837
Don't just throw yourself
into the hole like an idiot.

166
00:11:12,920 --> 00:11:15,214
Sorry, but I'm against you on this one.

167
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:17,577
Anybody could see it's an obvious trap.

168
00:11:17,660 --> 00:11:21,197
Don't even go near the thing until we can
find a clear connection between this deep,

169
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:24,456
dark abyss and the man who
got shot up in the hallway.

170
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:37,897
Whoever dug this hole started tunneling
to the side when they got deep enough.

171
00:11:37,980 --> 00:11:39,392
I can't see beyond that.

172
00:11:42,420 --> 00:11:46,677
The person that's accompanying Father
Poochie right now goes by the name Versus.

173
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:48,040
25, male.

174
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,675
Listen to me, Jolene.

175
00:11:49,780 --> 00:11:51,417
I said it before and I'll say it again.

176
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:53,217
I ain't going down in this damn hole.

177
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:54,917
Let's just wait for him to climb out.

178
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,257
Or we gotta find a way to
drag him out like rabbits.

179
00:11:57,340 --> 00:12:00,097
I'm already well aware that
this hole is an obvious trap.

180
00:12:00,180 --> 00:12:01,062
I'm not stupid.

181
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:04,337
But what happens if the priest is
planning to hole himself up down

182
00:12:04,420 --> 00:12:08,297
there for three more days while
he waits for the new moon to come?

183
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:09,210
No.

184
00:12:09,293 --> 00:12:10,780
Given how capable he is,

185
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,657
I bet Poochie and his accomplice plan to

186
00:12:12,740 --> 00:12:15,377
escape all the way to
Cape Canaveral like this.

187
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:16,400
In three days,

188
00:12:16,580 --> 00:12:18,757
that man's going to develop
some new ability that

189
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:21,457
will help him attain his
absurd idea of heaven.

190
00:12:21,540 --> 00:12:23,920
But for now, all he has is Pale Snake,

191
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:27,317
which merely allows him to
control the memories of others.

192
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:31,080
This is our chance if we
strike him now we can win

193
00:12:31,780 --> 00:12:35,157
We can't avoid it anymore if
we want to end this for good.

194
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:37,122
We might have to kill the priest

195
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:40,040
Hold on to this huh?

196
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:42,440
Don't let go no matter what

197
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:46,637
Hey, Joanne, what do
you think you're doing?

198
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:47,838
I'm coming with you

199
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:52,177
If we both go who's gonna stay
here to help pull me back up?

200
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:57,640
Take my rope and wrap it around your body
if I need help I'll signal You got it?

201
00:12:57,900 --> 00:13:00,194
Pull me out of here, whatever it takes.

202
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:02,000
She is crazy.

203
00:13:02,340 --> 00:13:03,860
But still though, Jolene,

204
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:06,537
if you keep pulling this
thread out of your body,

205
00:13:06,620 --> 00:13:09,679
just how far can you go
before you run out of slack?

206
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:22,890
Jolene!

207
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:25,500
Jolene! Hey!

208
00:13:25,820 --> 00:13:28,440
Why aren't you answering me? Jolene!

209
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:43,380
Where...am I?

210
00:13:52,220 --> 00:13:53,960
Where...am I?

211
00:13:56,980 --> 00:13:57,860
2005?!

212
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:00,980
What the...

213
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:08,760
Hey, look.

214
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:12,020
She came all this way
dragging her rope behind her.

215
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:14,720
I'll go cut it.

216
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:16,880
Fuck, not good.

217
00:14:17,140 --> 00:14:17,980
Where am I?

218
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:20,860
Hermes, hey! Can you hear me?

219
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:21,940
Things are bad!

220
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:24,340
Start pulling me up! Hurry!

221
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:25,620
Now, Hermes!

222
00:14:25,780 --> 00:14:26,662
I'm in trouble.

223
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:28,317
Please, get me out of here!

224
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:29,988
They're gonna cut the rope!

225
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:38,257
Come on, Hermes!

226
00:14:38,340 --> 00:14:39,811
What are you waiting for?

227
00:14:40,260 --> 00:14:41,200
Hurry, please!

228
00:14:42,180 --> 00:14:43,010
Hermes!

229
00:14:43,093 --> 00:14:44,662
Pull me out of the fucking hole!

230
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:47,870
Hermes!

231
00:14:48,940 --> 00:14:50,640
I know you can hear me!

232
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:58,937
Goddammit, what the ever-living
fuck is going on down there?

233
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:02,373
and she couldn't have really
gone that far into the hole!

234
00:15:07,220 --> 00:15:09,140
Go, Hermes! Keep pulling!

235
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:11,871
You're gonna have to pull me up even more!

236
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:23,280
I welcome you.

237
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:27,776
Even though you've come uninvited
and haven't greeted me, you may stay.

238
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:31,940
You chose to come into my hole
of your own volition. However,

239
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:37,145
I must insist the entirety of this tightly
pulled rope comes in with you as well.

240
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:39,900
Stone Ocean!

241
00:15:50,300 --> 00:15:53,240
Hey Versus, will you be alright?

242
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:57,777
Compared to you who has recently
developed a new stand ability,

243
00:15:57,860 --> 00:16:01,837
Jolene Kujo has undergone intense training
through her experiences in prison.

244
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:04,680
She is much more accustomed
to all-out battle.

245
00:16:05,060 --> 00:16:07,197
It's not surprising that she would steal a

246
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:09,417
pen from one of the
passengers on the plane.

247
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:11,840
Do not pursue Jolene any further.

248
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:14,440
You have done enough already, versus.

249
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:19,134
If Jolene wants to escape
from this hole, then so be it.

250
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:21,997
She won't attempt to
come back inside again.

251
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:23,551
At least not for a while.

252
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:26,337
For now, all we can do is wait patiently.

253
00:16:26,420 --> 00:16:29,008
We'll need to stay here
for three more days.

254
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:32,117
Can you hear me up there, Hermes?

255
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,494
I can see a light now!

256
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:35,377
I must be getting close to you!

257
00:16:35,460 --> 00:16:38,560
Pull me up even harder,
okay? Yeah! Jolene!

258
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:39,740
I can hear you!

259
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:42,477
And I'm starting to be able to see you!

260
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:43,390
Are you okay?

261
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:45,993
What the hell is down in this deep hole?

262
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:48,957
The enemy is staring
right at me as we speak!

263
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:50,800
Also, I could see the priest.

264
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:52,139
He's in here, too.

265
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:55,377
We have to come up with another
way for us to get down here again.

266
00:16:55,460 --> 00:16:58,284
It would have been over
if they'd cut this rope.

267
00:17:05,540 --> 00:17:07,900
Tell me something I want to know.

268
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:10,760
Hey, come on now, Hermes.

269
00:17:12,180 --> 00:17:13,237
How are you feeling?

270
00:17:13,320 --> 00:17:14,849
I'm just a little curious.

271
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:17,877
I really want to know.

272
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:21,497
How did it feel to get revenge on the
son of a bitch who murdered your sister?

273
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:23,977
Did you get some sort of
sick satisfaction out of

274
00:17:24,060 --> 00:17:26,657
burring me alive in that sewer
pipe you called an improv,

275
00:17:26,740 --> 00:17:27,570
Goffin?

276
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:30,640
It's Sports Maximum!

277
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:33,390
Hey!

278
00:17:33,473 --> 00:17:34,377
What's going on, Hermes?

279
00:17:34,460 --> 00:17:36,107
What are you doing up there?

280
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,020
Sorry, Jolene!

281
00:17:39,840 --> 00:17:43,397
The ground has a long memory of
everything that happens upon it.

282
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:47,540
Sort of like a tape recorder, or
even much like a digital camera.

283
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:48,860
For example,

284
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:51,317
it remembers that boy who was shot dead by

285
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:53,717
his own father when he
fell onto the ground.

286
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:55,437
Shit, where the hell are you?

287
00:17:55,520 --> 00:17:57,717
It even remembers the
gangster who was buried

288
00:17:57,800 --> 00:18:00,329
alive in a sewer pipe
and drowned to death.

289
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:04,097
The Earth's memory is so powerful that it
can even recall every single one of the

290
00:18:04,180 --> 00:18:09,062
passengers who met their demise on a plane
that fell to the ground in July of 2005,

291
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,160
six years ago.

292
00:18:10,660 --> 00:18:11,500
Hermes, hey!

293
00:18:11,740 --> 00:18:13,497
What the hell are you doing up there?

294
00:18:13,580 --> 00:18:16,577
Come on, Hermes! Stop! Let go of me!

295
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:21,357
I'm here thanks to versus stand ability
see netherworld uncovers all the

296
00:18:21,440 --> 00:18:25,675
folks who met the ground when they
perished and excavates their memories

297
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:26,790
Asshole!

298
00:18:33,520 --> 00:18:34,350
Joey!

299
00:18:40,740 --> 00:18:44,120
Excuse me, ladies. Welcome
aboard. Unfortunately,

300
00:18:44,260 --> 00:18:46,417
this plane is expected
to lose control and crash

301
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:51,000
into the ground at approximately
2133 on July Saudi, 2005.

302
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:54,397
We ask that you please turn
off all electronic devices,

303
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:59,068
and make sure that your seatbelt is
securely fastened around your lower waist.

304
00:18:59,920 --> 00:19:01,757
I suggest you heed that warning,

305
00:19:01,840 --> 00:19:05,840
or you'll end up like the man who
was sitting in the seat behind me.

306
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:10,195
His head was lodged straight
into my stomach on impact.

307
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:12,880
What? Ain't no way! Dammit!

308
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:14,257
Where's the entrance?

309
00:19:14,340 --> 00:19:15,557
Start looking, Hermes!

310
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:16,581
Help me find it!

311
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:18,640
Wait, what even is this place?

312
00:19:18,860 --> 00:19:20,742
Is this a hallucination, Jolene?

313
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,217
It should be on the ceiling.

314
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:24,359
Look for the place we came in from.

315
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:27,197
Everything in this fucking
plane feels so real, though.

316
00:19:27,280 --> 00:19:29,137
We need to find the way out of here now.

317
00:19:29,220 --> 00:19:32,297
Before you fell down, was there anyone
coming to check the room above the hall?

318
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:35,377
There was a panic in the halls
after that boy's dad was shot.

319
00:19:35,460 --> 00:19:37,297
The police had to have shown up.

320
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:38,520
Did you see anyone?

321
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:40,900
No, I have no clue. Besides,

322
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:43,437
even if the cops came, they
wouldn't be able to hear us calling,

323
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:45,937
just like I couldn't hear
you up there earlier.

324
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:47,577
How's this plane down here anyway?

325
00:19:47,660 --> 00:19:52,366
I didn't see anything like this when I
was waiting for you to come out the hall.

326
00:19:53,940 --> 00:19:56,817
Excuse me, miss, please refrain
from punching the ceiling.

327
00:19:56,900 --> 00:20:00,018
If you would, kindly take
your seat and wait quietly.

328
00:20:00,660 --> 00:20:03,895
This plane will be crashing
in less than three minutes.

329
00:20:05,220 --> 00:20:07,120
Okay, then let us see the pilot!

330
00:20:07,380 --> 00:20:09,577
We gotta make him land
this plane immediately!

331
00:20:09,660 --> 00:20:12,425
Now hurry up, lady, and
take us to the cockpit!

332
00:20:12,860 --> 00:20:13,690
No point.

333
00:20:18,740 --> 00:20:21,037
We weren't able to land the plane safely.

334
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:23,860
That's the reason why we crashed!

335
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:31,997
Unfortunately for us, we all burned
to death when the plane crash landed.

336
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:35,677
It exploded and That was when my body

337
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:40,497
um excuse me sir did you not hear me

338
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:44,757
when I told everyone to turn off of all
of their electronic devices earlier?

339
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:45,720
Could it be?

340
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:47,800
I think I remember this.

341
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:50,380
It was flight number 2882 to Dallas.

342
00:20:50,660 --> 00:20:53,977
Around six or seven years ago, it
crashed somewhere near Orlando.

343
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:55,717
We're dealing with ghosts here.

344
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:57,160
No, we're memories.

345
00:20:57,480 --> 00:20:58,420
That's all.

346
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:01,517
Remnants of memories that
were recorded by the Earth.

347
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:05,541
Are you trying to tell me we're
actually gonna crash in this thing?

348
00:21:09,780 --> 00:21:12,860
Can you not make this plane
crash happen any faster?

349
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:17,501
I've been sensing weather forecasts
getting closer to our position.

350
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:29,277
It appears that he is drawing
ever closer toward this hospital.

351
00:21:29,360 --> 00:21:34,760
I swear to God, if you don't shut the fuck
up already and stop confusing me, Huh.

352
00:21:35,140 --> 00:21:36,600
Were you speaking to me?

353
00:21:41,740 --> 00:21:45,387
Netherworld's ability is to
excavate memories from the ground.

354
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:50,220
And this plane is set to crash
specifically at 2133 on the dot.

355
00:21:50,760 --> 00:21:51,590
Also,

356
00:21:51,673 --> 00:21:53,257
try not to forget that
I've capitalized on this

357
00:21:53,340 --> 00:21:56,811
opportunity and managed to pull
Ermes into my hole as well.

358
00:21:58,160 --> 00:22:00,336
I have done this all for you, Father.

359
00:22:01,120 --> 00:22:02,960
Now just leave it to me.

360
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:30,180
Although you think I cope

361
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:34,380
My head is filled with hope

362
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:40,057
Of some place

363
00:22:40,140 --> 00:22:43,800
other than here

364
00:22:46,540 --> 00:22:50,200
Although you think I smile

365
00:22:51,780 --> 00:22:55,280
Inside and all the while

366
00:22:57,060 --> 00:23:03,460
I'm wondering about my destiny?

367
00:23:05,940 --> 00:23:07,937
I'm thinking

368
00:23:08,020 --> 00:23:13,597
about all the

369
00:23:13,680 --> 00:23:18,457
things I'd like

370
00:23:18,540 --> 00:23:24,540
to do in my life.

371
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:29,297
I'm a dreamer.

372
00:23:29,380 --> 00:23:34,460
A distant dreamer.

373
00:23:36,380 --> 00:23:39,420
Dreaming far away.

374
00:23:41,760 --> 00:23:44,560
From today!

375
00:23:54,540 --> 00:23:55,370
Thank you.

376
00:24:24,540 --> 00:24:26,340
Thank you.
